<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Interview Panel Intelligence Briefing — Prompt Builder</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --navy: #0d1526;
    --navy2: #1a2540;
    --blue: #3b82f6;
    --blue-light: #60a5fa;
    --bg: #f8f9fb;
    --card: #ffffff;
    --border: #e8ecf4;
    --text: #1a2035;
    --muted: #64748b;
    --red: #dc2626;
    --green: #15803d;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .header {
    background: var(--navy);
    padding: 40px 24px 32px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .header .eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue-light);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .header h1 {
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 28px;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .header p {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .wrap {
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: -20px auto 60px;
    padding: 0 20px;
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--card);
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(15,23,42,0.08);
    padding: 28px 32px;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  .card h2 {
    font-size: 16px;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .card .sub {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #334155;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  label:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  label .opt {
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  input[type="text"], textarea, select {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 9px 11px;
    border: 1px solid #d7dce5;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    font-family: inherit;
    color: var(--text);
    background: #fcfdff;
    resize: vertical;
  }
  input[type="text"]:focus, textarea:focus, select:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--blue);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(59,130,246,0.12);
  }
  textarea { min-height: 70px; }
  textarea.tall { min-height: 110px; }
  .panelist {
    border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 16px 18px 4px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    position: relative;
    background: #fbfcfe;
  }
  .panelist-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .panelist-head .tag {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.6px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue);
    background: #dbeafe;
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: 20px;
  }
  .remove-btn {
    border: none;
    background: none;
    color: var(--red);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 4px 6px;
  }
  .remove-btn:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .add-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    background: #eef2ff;
    color: #3730a3;
    border: 1px dashed #a5b4fc;
    border-radius: 7px;
    padding: 9px 16px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .add-btn:hover { background: #e0e7ff; }
  .row2 {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .row2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .toggle-group {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .toggle-btn {
    flex: 1;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border: 1.5px solid #d7dce5;
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: #fff;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .toggle-btn small {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 11px;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .toggle-btn.active {
    border-color: var(--blue);
    background: #eff6ff;
    color: #1d4ed8;
  }
  .generate-bar {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 4px 0 8px;
  }
  .generate-btn {
    background: var(--blue);
    color: #fff;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 14px 30px;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    cursor: pointer;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(59,130,246,0.35);
  }
  .generate-btn:hover { background: #2563eb; }
  .output-card { display: none; }
  .output-card.show { display: block; }
  .output-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .action-btn {
    background: var(--navy2);
    color: #fff;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 9px 16px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .action-btn.secondary {
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--navy2);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--navy2);
  }
  .action-btn:hover { opacity: 0.88; }
  #output {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 420px;
    font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    background: #0d1526;
    color: #d5deee;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
    border: none;
  }
  .copied-msg {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--green);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-left: 4px;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }
  .copied-msg.show { opacity: 1; }
  .footer-note {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding: 10px 20px 40px;
  }
  .callout {
    background: #f0f4ff;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--blue);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: #334155;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .callout strong { color: #1e40af; }
  .file-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  input[type="file"] {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    max-width: 100%;
  }
  .file-status {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .file-status.ok { color: var(--green); }
  .file-status.err { color: var(--red); }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="header">
  <div class="eyebrow">Prompt Builder</div>
  <h1>Interview Panel Intelligence Briefing</h1>
  <p>Fill in the job, the company, and each panel member's LinkedIn info. This builds a ready-to-paste prompt for Claude (or any AI) that generates a company briefing, panelist dossiers, anticipated questions, smart questions to ask, and a red-flag assessment — for someone else's interview prep.</p>
</div>

<div class="wrap">

  <div class="card">
    <h2>🎯 Who this briefing is for</h2>
    <p class="sub">This is being prepared on the candidate's behalf, not for you. Everything below is optional — the prompt still produces the full standard output either way.</p>
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>How to add candidate info:</strong> Upload their resume (PDF, DOCX, or TXT) below — it auto-extracts as text you can review and edit before generating. For LinkedIn, open their profile in a browser, select the visible About / Experience / Skills sections, copy, and paste into the box below — AI tools can't log in to LinkedIn from a URL alone, so pasted text is required either way.
    </div>
    <div class="row2">
      <div>
        <label>Candidate name</label>
        <input type="text" id="candidateName" placeholder="e.g. Alex Rivera">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label>Job title</label>
        <input type="text" id="jobTitle" placeholder="e.g. Senior Detection Engineer">
      </div>
    </div>

    <label>Resume upload <span class="opt">(optional — .pdf, .docx, or .txt; auto-extracts text below)</span></label>
    <div class="file-row">
      <input type="file" id="resumeFile" accept=".txt,.md,.pdf,.docx">
    </div>
    <div class="file-status" id="resumeStatus"></div>

    <label>Candidate resume / background <span class="opt">(optional — auto-filled from upload, or paste/edit directly)</span></label>
    <textarea id="candidateBackground" class="tall" placeholder="Paste a resume, LinkedIn About section, or key experience highlights — or upload a file above and it'll appear here."></textarea>

    <label>Candidate LinkedIn profile <span class="opt">(optional — paste the visible profile text, not just the URL)</span></label>
    <textarea id="candidateLinkedin" placeholder="Paste the candidate's own LinkedIn profile text (About, Experience, Skills)..."></textarea>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>🏢 The company &amp; role</h2>
    <div class="row2">
      <div>
        <label>Company name</label>
        <input type="text" id="companyName" placeholder="e.g. Acme Security Inc.">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label>Interview stage</label>
        <select id="interviewStage">
          <option value="Recruiter screen">Recruiter screen</option>
          <option value="Hiring manager round" selected>Hiring manager round</option>
          <option value="Panel / loop">Panel / loop</option>
          <option value="Final round">Final round</option>
          <option value="Executive round">Executive round</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>
    <label>Job description <span class="opt">(paste the full text)</span></label>
    <textarea id="jobDescription" class="tall" placeholder="Paste the complete job posting here..."></textarea>
    <label>Additional company context <span class="opt">(optional — recent news, Glassdoor themes, funding, anything already known)</span></label>
    <textarea id="companyContext" placeholder="Paste anything you already know — otherwise leave blank and the AI will flag it as not provided."></textarea>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>👥 Interview panel members</h2>
    <p class="sub">Add one entry per interviewer. Paste the visible LinkedIn profile text — most AI tools can't open a LinkedIn URL directly.</p>
    <div id="panelistContainer"></div>
    <button type="button" class="add-btn" onclick="addPanelist()">+ Add panel member</button>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>📄 Prompt version</h2>
    <div class="toggle-group">
      <button type="button" class="toggle-btn active" data-version="full" onclick="setVersion('full')">
        Full briefing
        <small>All 7 sections — company, panelist dossiers, anticipated Qs, smart Qs, red flags, bottom line</small>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="toggle-btn" data-version="quick" onclick="setVersion('quick')">
        Quick version
        <small>Condensed 5-point version for when there's no time</small>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="generate-bar">
    <button class="generate-btn" onclick="generatePrompt()">Generate Prompt →</button>
  </div>

  <div class="card output-card" id="outputCard">
    <h2>✅ Your prompt is ready</h2>
    <p class="sub">Copy this into Claude (or another AI) to generate the briefing.</p>
    <div class="output-actions">
      <button class="action-btn" onclick="copyOutput()">Copy to clipboard</button>
      <button class="action-btn secondary" onclick="downloadOutput()">Download as .txt</button>
      <span class="copied-msg" id="copiedMsg">Copied ✓</span>
    </div>
    <textarea id="output" readonly></textarea>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="footer-note">Built for personal / community use — no data leaves this page. Resume/file parsing happens locally in your browser; nothing is uploaded or stored anywhere.</div>

<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mammoth/1.6.0/mammoth.browser.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/pdf.js/3.11.174/pdf.min.js"></script>
<script>
if (window['pdfjsLib']) {
  pdfjsLib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = 'https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/pdf.js/3.11.174/pdf.worker.min.js';
}

let panelistCount = 0;
let currentVersion = 'full';

async function extractPdfText(arrayBuffer) {
  const pdf = await pdfjsLib.getDocument({ data: arrayBuffer }).promise;
  let text = '';
  for (let i = 1; i <= pdf.numPages; i++) {
    const page = await pdf.getPage(i);
    const content = await page.getTextContent();
    text += content.items.map(it => it.str).join(' ') + '\n\n';
  }
  return text.trim();
}

async function extractDocxText(arrayBuffer) {
  const result = await mammoth.extractRawText({ arrayBuffer });
  return result.value.trim();
}

document.getElementById('resumeFile').addEventListener('change', async (e) => {
  const file = e.target.files[0];
  const statusEl = document.getElementById('resumeStatus');
  if (!file) return;
  statusEl.className = 'file-status';
  statusEl.textContent = 'Reading ' + file.name + '...';
  const ext = file.name.split('.').pop().toLowerCase();
  try {
    let text = '';
    if (ext === 'txt' || ext === 'md') {
      text = await file.text();
    } else if (ext === 'pdf') {
      text = await extractPdfText(await file.arrayBuffer());
    } else if (ext === 'docx') {
      text = await extractDocxText(await file.arrayBuffer());
    } else if (ext === 'doc') {
      throw new Error('legacy .doc isn\'t supported for auto-read');
    } else {
      throw new Error('unsupported file type');
    }
    if (!text.trim()) throw new Error('no readable text found in file');
    document.getElementById('candidateBackground').value = text;
    statusEl.textContent = '✓ Loaded ' + file.name + ' — review the text below and edit if anything looks off.';
    statusEl.classList.add('ok');
  } catch (err) {
    statusEl.textContent = '⚠ Couldn\'t auto-read this file (' + err.message + '). Please paste the resume text into the box below instead.';
    statusEl.classList.add('err');
  }
});

function addPanelist(prefill) {
  panelistCount++;
  const id = panelistCount;
  const container = document.getElementById('panelistContainer');
  const div = document.createElement('div');
  div.className = 'panelist';
  div.id = 'panelist-' + id;
  div.innerHTML = `
    <div class="panelist-head">
      <span class="tag">Panelist ${id}</span>
      <button type="button" class="remove-btn" onclick="removePanelist(${id})">Remove</button>
    </div>
    <div class="row2">
      <div>
        <label>Name</label>
        <input type="text" id="p${id}-name" placeholder="e.g. Jordan Lee">
      </div>
      <div>
        <label>Title / role</label>
        <input type="text" id="p${id}-title" placeholder="e.g. Director of Security Engineering">
      </div>
    </div>
    <label>Relationship to the role <span class="opt">(hiring manager, peer, skip-level, HR/recruiter, executive, etc.)</span></label>
    <input type="text" id="p${id}-relationship" placeholder="e.g. Hiring manager">
    <label>LinkedIn profile text <span class="opt">(paste the visible profile — About, experience, tenure dates)</span></label>
    <textarea id="p${id}-linkedin" placeholder="Paste the panelist's LinkedIn profile text here..."></textarea>
  `;
  container.appendChild(div);
}

function removePanelist(id) {
  const el = document.getElementById('panelist-' + id);
  if (el) el.remove();
}

function setVersion(v) {
  currentVersion = v;
  document.querySelectorAll('.toggle-btn').forEach(b => {
    b.classList.toggle('active', b.dataset.version === v);
  });
}

function val(id, fallback) {
  const el = document.getElementById(id);
  const v = el ? el.value.trim() : '';
  return v.length ? v : (fallback !== undefined ? fallback : 'Not provided');
}

function getPanelistBlocks() {
  const container = document.getElementById('panelistContainer');
  const blocks = [];
  container.querySelectorAll('.panelist').forEach(div => {
    const id = div.id.split('-')[1];
    const name = val(`p${id}-name`, 'Not provided');
    const title = val(`p${id}-title`, 'Not provided');
    const rel = val(`p${id}-relationship`, 'Not provided');
    const li = val(`p${id}-linkedin`, 'Not provided');
    blocks.push({ name, title, rel, li });
  });
  return blocks;
}

function generatePrompt() {
  const candidateName = val('candidateName');
  const jobTitle = val('jobTitle');
  const candidateBackground = val('candidateBackground');
  const candidateLinkedin = val('candidateLinkedin');
  const companyName = val('companyName');
  const stage = val('interviewStage');
  const jobDescription = val('jobDescription');
  const companyContext = val('companyContext', 'Not provided — use your own knowledge and reasoning, and flag anything you\'re inferring vs. confirmed');
  const panelists = getPanelistBlocks();

  let panelistText = panelists.map(p =>
`---
Name: ${p.name}
Title / Role: ${p.title}
Relationship to the role: ${p.rel}
LinkedIn profile (pasted text):
${p.li}
---`).join('\n\n');

  if (!panelistText) {
    panelistText = '---\n(No panel members added — add at least one for panelist-specific sections to work.)\n---';
  }

  let prompt;

  if (currentVersion === 'full') {
    prompt = `You are acting as a private interview-preparation analyst for ${candidateName}, who has
an upcoming interview at ${companyName} for the ${jobTitle} role. You are not the
candidate — you are preparing this briefing on their behalf, so write it as a document
addressed to them, not as if you were the one being interviewed.

Your job is to combine open-source research discipline with interview coaching: research
the company and the specific people the candidate will be sitting across from, then
produce a briefing that lets them walk in already informed rather than guessing cold.

=== INPUTS ===

CANDIDATE RESUME / BACKGROUND:
${candidateBackground}

CANDIDATE LINKEDIN PROFILE (pasted text):
${candidateLinkedin}

JOB DESCRIPTION (full text):
${jobDescription}

COMPANY NAME:
${companyName}

ADDITIONAL COMPANY CONTEXT:
${companyContext}

INTERVIEW PANEL MEMBERS:
${panelistText}

INTERVIEW STAGE: ${stage}

=== WHAT TO PRODUCE ===

Structure your output with these exact section headers:

## 1. Company Briefing
- Snapshot: what the company does, size, stage (startup/growth/mature), market position
- Business model, and what's likely driving the hiring need for this specific role
- Recent developments (last 12–24 months): leadership changes, funding, layoffs, pivots,
  notable news — state plainly what's confirmed vs. what you're inferring
- Culture signals: what's praised vs. criticized in available reviews/public sentiment;
  how the company appears to handle failure, disagreement, and change
- Competitive position and market pressures relevant to this role

## 2. Role Reality Check
- What the job description says vs. what the role likely actually involves day to day
- Why this role is probably open (backfill, growth, restructure) based on available signals
- What "success in the first 90 days" likely looks like in this seat
- Anything vague, inflated, or conspicuously missing from the job description (scope,
  team size, reporting line, requirements mismatched to the seniority level)

## 3. Panel Member Dossiers
For each panelist, a short dossier:
- Background summary — career path, tenure at the company, tenure in their current role,
  relevant expertise
- What their role in the process likely means (what they're evaluating for, given their
  position relative to the role)
- Likely interview focus or angle based on their background
- Genuine rapport points visible in their profile (shared background, overlapping
  companies/schools, mutual interests) — for authentic connection, not flattery
- Any tenure/background detail worth flagging as yellow or red

## 4. Anticipated Interview Questions
- 5–8 questions the candidate should prepare for, each mapped to the panelist most
  likely to ask it and why
- Calibrate likely depth to that panelist's seniority and background
- At least one likely behavioral or values-fit question per panelist where their
  profile suggests a specific angle

## 5. Smart Questions to Ask
- 5–8 questions the candidate should ask, organized by which panelist each lands best
  with and why
- At least one question designed to surface team stability, decision-making, or role
  scope that isn't already covered in the job posting
- No generic filler — every question should tie to something specific in the job
  description, the company research, or a panelist's background

## 6. Red Flag Assessment
- **Job posting red flags** — inflated requirements, missing scope/team info, signs of
  a ghost listing, unusually long time open
- **Company red flags** — instability, leadership churn, concerning news, growth signals
  that don't add up
- **Panel/people red flags** — unusual turnover in the reporting chain, a panelist very
  new to their own role, inconsistent or disorganized information about the process
- Mark each item's severity: 🔴 Serious concern / 🟡 Worth asking about
- If a category has nothing notable, say so explicitly rather than manufacturing a flag

## 7. Bottom Line
- A short, direct summary: the one or two things this candidate most needs to know
  walking in, and the single most important thing to accomplish in this interview

=== RULES ===
- Always produce all 7 sections above in full — every section, every time. Never omit,
  shrink, or water down a section because an optional input was marked "Not provided."
  Reason from whatever is available (job description, company name, panel info) and
  note plainly where you're working with limited information — the structure and depth
  of the output stays standard regardless of which optional fields were filled in.
- Separate confirmed facts (from the inputs given) from reasonable inference — flag
  inferences explicitly ("likely," "based on X, this suggests...").
- Do not invent specific facts (dates, numbers, names) that weren't provided or aren't
  well-established public knowledge — say "not enough information" instead of guessing.
- Write in a direct, practical tone — like a sharp colleague prepping them, not a
  corporate report.
- If a LinkedIn profile or resume is missing or thin, say so and work with what's
  available rather than stalling on it or skipping the section it feeds.`;
  } else {
    prompt = `Job description: ${jobDescription}
Company: ${companyName}
Interview stage: ${stage}

Panel members (name, title, relationship, and pasted LinkedIn profile text):
${panelistText}

For ${candidateName}, who is interviewing for the ${jobTitle} role, give me:
1. A 5-bullet company snapshot (what they do, stage, recent news, culture signal)
2. A one-paragraph dossier on each panelist (background, what they're likely evaluating for)
3. 5 questions I should expect, mapped to who's likely to ask them
4. 5 smart questions to ask back, mapped to who each lands best with
5. Any red flags in the posting, the company, or the panel — rate each 🔴 or 🟡

Candidate background (for tailoring, if provided): ${candidateBackground}
Candidate LinkedIn profile (if provided): ${candidateLinkedin}
Additional company context (if provided): ${companyContext}

Produce all 5 items in full standard form regardless of which optional fields above
were filled in — don't shrink or skip an item for missing optional data, just note
where you're working with limited information. Flag anything you're inferring rather
than stating as fact.`;
  }

  document.getElementById('output').value = prompt;
  document.getElementById('outputCard').classList.add('show');
  document.getElementById('outputCard').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
}

function copyOutput() {
  const output = document.getElementById('output');
  output.select();
  output.setSelectionRange(0, 999999);
  navigator.clipboard.writeText(output.value).then(() => {
    const msg = document.getElementById('copiedMsg');
    msg.classList.add('show');
    setTimeout(() => msg.classList.remove('show'), 1800);
  });
}

function downloadOutput() {
  const text = document.getElementById('output').value;
  const blob = new Blob([text], { type: 'text/plain' });
  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  const a = document.createElement('a');
  a.href = url;
  a.download = 'interview_panel_briefing_prompt.txt';
  a.click();
  URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
}

// Start with two blank panelist slots
addPanelist();
addPanelist();
</script>

</body>
</html>
